{"id":9141092,"docketId":66407387,"caseName":"In re Disbarment of Rogers","caseNameFull":"In re Disbarment of Rogers","slug":"in-re-disbarment-of-rogers","docketNumber":"No. D-1306","dateFiled":"1993-11-15","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1993,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":0,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":9135770,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":544,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<p id=\"AX5n\">John I. Rogers</p>\n<p id=\"Aq09\">III, of Bennettsville, S. C., having requested to resign as a member of the Bar of this Court, it is ordered that his name be stricken from the roll of attorneys admitted to practice before the <page-number citation-index=\"1\" label=\"974\">*974</page-number>Bar of this Court. The rule to show cause, heretofore issued on September 24, 1993 [<span class=\"citation multiple-matches\"><a href=\"/c/U.%20S./509/949/\">509 U. S. 949</a></span>], is hereby discharged.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}